    {
      "id": "lB6mPSqy3qP-Oi3zDslIa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 344,
      "y": 242,
      "width": 629.9395751953125,
      "height": 1625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 758089680,
      "version": 1296,
      "versionNonce": 1799783728,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1765627474301,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- The Backend is the single source of truth\n\n. Scenario 1 - User pays , frontend closes !\n\n-- What happens ?\n\n- Payment succeeds on Stripe\n- User close tab / Internet issues\n- Frontend  never use /success\n\n-- Risks\n\n- Order remains unPaid\n- Money already taken\n\n-- Solutions\n\n- Backend Solution : Webhook \n\n. Scenario 2 - Payment fails (card declined)\n\n-- What happens?\n- Stripe rejects payment\n\n-- Risk \n- Order stuck in pending state\n\n- Backend Solution : payment_intent.payment_failed\n==> Mark order as failed\n==> Notify user\n\n. Scenario 3 - Webhook sent multiple times\n\n-- What happens ?\n- Stripe retries webhook on failure\n\n--Risks\n- Order marked paid twice\n- Stock decreased twice\n\n- Backend Solution : \n- Check if order is already paid\n\n. Scenario 4 : Two users buy the same product at the same time\n\n-- What happens ?\n- Product stock = 1\n- Two users checkout in the same time\n\n- Frontend solution : stock check (Bad Solution)\n\n- Backend Solution (Atomic operation):\n\n- Reduce stock only if payment success\n\n- Use MongoDB atomic update : \n\nProduct.findOneAndUpdate(\n { _id : productId , stock : { $gte : quantity } },\n { $inc : { stock : -quantity } }\n)\n\n\n \n   ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- The Backend is the single source of truth\n\n. Scenario 1 - User pays , frontend closes !\n\n-- What happens ?\n\n- Payment succeeds on Stripe\n- User close tab / Internet issues\n- Frontend  never use /success\n\n-- Risks\n\n- Order remains unPaid\n- Money already taken\n\n-- Solutions\n\n- Backend Solution : Webhook \n\n. Scenario 2 - Payment fails (card declined)\n\n-- What happens?\n- Stripe rejects payment\n\n-- Risk \n- Order stuck in pending state\n\n- Backend Solution : payment_intent.payment_failed\n==> Mark order as failed\n==> Notify user\n\n. Scenario 3 - Webhook sent multiple times\n\n-- What happens ?\n- Stripe retries webhook on failure\n\n--Risks\n- Order marked paid twice\n- Stock decreased twice\n\n- Backend Solution : \n- Check if order is already paid\n\n. Scenario 4 : Two users buy the same product at the same time\n\n-- What happens ?\n- Product stock = 1\n- Two users checkout in the same time\n\n- Frontend solution : stock check (Bad Solution)\n\n- Backend Solution (Atomic operation):\n\n- Reduce stock only if payment success\n\n- Use MongoDB atomic update : \n\nProduct.findOneAndUpdate(\n { _id : productId , stock : { $gte : quantity } },\n { $inc : { stock : -quantity } }\n)\n\n\n \n   ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
