      "text": "Rule : Never trust read then write logic\nuse : atomic operations",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Rule : Never trust read then write logic\nuse : atomic operations",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uKF1zUgJHxmWVbhsGGeZg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 354,
      "y": 2200,
      "width": 484.97918701171875,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1197545424,
      "version": 577,
      "versionNonce": 844537136,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1765627317814,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-----------------------------------------------------------\n\nStock = 1\nReserved = 0\nAvailable = Stock - Reserved = 1\n\nUser A request (arrives first)\n\nProduct.findOneAndUpdate(\n { _id : productId , \n    stock : { $gte : quantity + reserved } },\n { $inc : { reserved: quantity } }\n)\n==> Reserved becomes 1\nStock = 1\nReserved = 1\nAvailable = Stock - Reserved = 0\n\nUser B request (arrives ms later)\n\nstock >= quantity + reserved\n1 >= 1 + 1 : Condition fails\n==> Update does NOT happen\n========> Out of Stock\n\n-Why this works ????\n--- Only one update can succeed\n--- No two users can reserve the same stock",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-----------------------------------------------------------\n\nStock = 1\nReserved = 0\nAvailable = Stock - Reserved = 1\n\nUser A request (arrives first)\n\nProduct.findOneAndUpdate(\n { _id : productId , \n    stock : { $gte : quantity + reserved } },\n { $inc : { reserved: quantity } }\n)\n==> Reserved becomes 1\nStock = 1\nReserved = 1\nAvailable = Stock - Reserved = 0\n\nUser B request (arrives ms later)\n\nstock >= quantity + reserved\n1 >= 1 + 1 : Condition fails\n==> Update does NOT happen\n========> Out of Stock\n\n-Why this works ????\n--- Only one update can succeed\n--- No two users can reserve the same stock",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "d_fOcLsYukKMoJz4tbWAd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 346.6298370361328,
      "y": 3114,
      "width": 556.379638671875,
      "height": 850,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 322824741,
      "version": 568,
      "versionNonce": 1106742347,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1765996346841,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Scenario 5 : User creates order but never pays\n\nWhat happens ? \n\n- Order created\n- Payment not completed\n\nRisks \n\n- Stock blocked\n\nBackend Solution : \n\n- Do not reduce stock on order creation\n- Reduce stock only after webhook payment confirmation\n\n\nScenario 6 : User modifies price on frontend\n\nWhat happens ?\n\n- User changes price in request payload\n\nRisks\n\n- Free or cheaper orders\n\nBackend Solution :\n\n- Calculate total price on backend\n- Fetch product prices from databases\n- Ignore frontend totals\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Scenario 5 : User creates order but never pays\n\nWhat happens ? \n\n- Order created\n- Payment not completed\n\nRisks \n\n- Stock blocked\n\nBackend Solution : \n\n- Do not reduce stock on order creation\n- Reduce stock only after webhook payment confirmation\n\n\nScenario 6 : User modifies price on frontend\n\nWhat happens ?\n\n- User changes price in request payload\n\nRisks\n\n- Free or cheaper orders\n\nBackend Solution :\n\n- Calculate total price on backend\n- Fetch product prices from databases\n- Ignore frontend totals\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
